WEBVTT

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.920
Anchor! Chum!

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.800
There you are, Bruce. Finally.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.680
-We got company.
-It's about time, mate.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.600
We've gone through the snacks
and I'm starving.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.840
We almost had to have
a feeding frenzy.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.560
Let's get this over with.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.280
(DING)

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.120
Right then. The meeting has
officially come to order.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.880
Let us all say the pledge.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.800
ALL: I am a nice shark,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.240
not a mindless eating machine.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.000
If I am to change this image,
I must first change myself.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.760
Fish are friends, not food.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.440
Except stinking dolphins.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.440
Dolphins!
Yeah, they think they're so cute.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.640
Look, I'm a flipping little dolphin.
Let me flip for you. Ain't I something?

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.280
Today's meeting is step five:
Bring a Fish Friend.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.560
-Do you all have your friends?
-Got mine.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.080
DORY: Hey there!
BRUCE: How about you, Chum?

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.880
Well, I seem to have misplaced my

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.560
friend.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.600
BRUCE: It's all right, Chum.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.600
Help yourself to one of my friends.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.200
Thanks, mate. A little chum for Chum.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.920
I'll start the testimonies.
Hello. My name is Bruce.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.200
Hello, Bruce.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.440
It has been three weeks
since my last fish, on my honor,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.840
or may I be chopped up
and made into soup.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.720
-You're an inspiration to us.
-Amen.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.680
-Right, then. Who's next?
-Pick me. Pick me.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.600
-The little sheila down the front.
-Whoo!

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.960
Come on up here.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.600
Hi. I'm Dory.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.280
Hello, Dory.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.680
And... Well, I don't think
I've ever eaten a fish.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.800
-Hey, that's incredible.
-Good on you, mate!

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.840
I'm glad I got that off my chest.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.160
Anyone else? How about you, mate?
What's your problem?

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.560
Me? I don't have a problem.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.120
-Okay.
-ALL: Denial.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.480
Just start with your name.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.880
Okay. Hello.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.960
My name is Marlin. I'm a clownfish.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.560
-A clownfish? Really?
-Go on. Tell us a joke.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.800
I love jokes.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.080
I actually do know
one that's pretty good.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.640
There was this mollusk
and he walks up to a sea cucumber.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.120
Normally they don't talk,
but in a joke, everyone talks.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.240
The sea mollusk
says to the cucumber...

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.040
Daddy!

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.600
Nemo!

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.840
Nemo! (LAUGHS)

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.920
-I don't get it.
-For a clownfish he's not that funny.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.440
No, he's my son.
He was taken by these divers.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.000
You poor fish.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.360
-Humans. Think they own everything.
-Probably American.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.560
(TEARFULLY) There is a father
looking for his little boy.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.680
MARLIN:
What do these markings mean?

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.640
-(SOBS) I never knew my father.
-Come here.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.840
-We're all mates here.
-I can't read human.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.960
Then we've got to find a fish
that can read this. Look. Sharks!

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.400
-Guys.
-No, Dory.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.840
-That's mine. Give it back.
-Cut it out.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.600
-Ow!
-I'm sorry. Are you okay?

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.560
You really clocked me there.
Am I bleeding?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.520
Dory, are you oka... (SNIFFS)

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.120
Oh!

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.720
That's good.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.640
Intervention!

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.280
-Just a bite.
-You hold it together, mate.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.240
-Fish are friends, not food.
-Food!

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.840
Dory, look out.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.760
I'm having fish tonight.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.120
Remember the steps, mate.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.200
Just one bite.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.800
G'day.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.080
There's no way out.
There's got to be a way to escape.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.080
-Who is it?
-Help me find a way out.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.920
Sorry. You'll have to come back later.
We're trying to escape.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.400
There's no way out.
There's got to be a way out.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.680
Here's something. "Es-ca-pé."
I wonder what that means.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.840
-It's spelled just like the word "escape."
-Let's go.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.000
Here's Brucie!

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:26.120
-Wait a minute. You can read?
-I can read? That's right!

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.720
Then here. Read this now.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.760
He doesn't mean it.
He never even knew his father.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.840
Don't fall off the wagon.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.400
Oh, no! It's blocked.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.080
No, Bruce!

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.600
Sorry about... Bruce, mate.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.920
He's really... A nice guy.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.560
I need to get that mask.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.120
You want that mask? Okay.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.560
No, no, no, no!

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.200
Quick. Grab the mask.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.240
Oh, no. Bruce.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.520
What?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.400
Swim away!

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:13.880
DORY: Is the party over?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:14.960
(PING)

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.080
Nice.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.080
Dad!

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.080
Daddy?

